From 9744578a42210eb50d15befe94b01573af77faf5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:01:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(plugins): plugin activation reaches every chat-hosting
 backend, not just the host owner [daveey]

notify_serve_backend() dialed only the first live serve record (host owner, else Desktop child).
On a host running both (laptop-1: hermes serve :9119 plus the Desktop child), the Desktop child,
which hosts the Desktop chats, never got re-activated, so those chats ran plugin hooks loaded at
its start (example-card).

- serve_backend_records(): every live, token-consistent serve / desktop-serve record.
- notify_serve_backend_record(): one backend; notify_serve_backends(): per-backend answers.
- notify_serve_backend(): fans out, folds answers (host owner first) with a 'backends' list and
  a backend_error naming each failed <role>:<port>, so a failed Desktop child is never reported
  as loaded. A dead, torn-token or unreachable record never blocks the others.
- _serve_backend_record() kept (first record) for older hermes-sync callers.
